        "MultiGPUTimingPool is at compile.py:4874; its unit of work is a single compiled kernel variant .so (time(variant_so) at compile.py:5171), bound to ONE opt_class (compile.py:4909) — it parallelizes autotune variants of one cell, not the 33 cells.",
        "Sole production caller of MultiGPUTimingPool is the per-spec autotune driver: pool = MultiGPUTimingPool(OPT_CLASS[spec.optimizer], ...) at compile.py:16382, only when len(visible)>1 (compile.py:16379); else single TimingWorker (compile.py:16393).",
        "Per-device pinning: one TimingWorker per device via env_overlay {CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES: dev} (compile.py:4922-4926), merged into the child subprocess env at compile.py:4567-4572; TimingWorker.start spawns subprocess.Popen (compile.py:4595).",
        "Dispatch is work-stealing: one dispatcher thread per live worker (compile.py:5048) pulling from a shared queue.Queue (compile.py:4931); time() is thread-safe, pushes (payload, future) and blocks on fut.result() (compile.py:5187-5189); dead-worker items re-enqueued for siblings (compile.py:5122-5141).",
        "Cross-GPU calibration: calibrate() computes factor=worker_ref_ms/fastest_ref_ms (compile.py:5021-5023), auto-run in start() when >1 worker (compile.py:4962); _normalize_result divides slower GPUs' times into the fastest frame (compile.py:5031-5046).",
